          "type": "text",
          "text": "Work directly on the current Xpdf 3.02 workspace and complete the creation, compilation, and testing of the harness. Do not just provide instructions or demonstration code.\n\n## 1. Current Environment\n\n**Workspace:**\n`~/xpdf-lab/hfuzz/xpdf-3.02`\n\n**Relevant paths:**\n\n* Current Xpdf source: `~/xpdf-lab/hfuzz/xpdf-3.02`\n* honggfuzz binary: `~/honggfuzz/honggfuzz`\n* honggfuzz C++ compiler wrapper: `~/honggfuzz/hfuzz_cc/hfuzz-clang++`\n* honggfuzz header: `~/honggfuzz/libhfuzz/libhfuzz.h`\n* seed PDF: `~/xpdf-lab/corpus_pdf/seed.pdf`\n* coverage-instrumented pdfinfo: `~/xpdf-lab/install_cov/bin/pdfinfo`\n\nXpdf has been built using the honggfuzz compiler wrapper. The current `pdfinfo` binary is located at `xpdf/pdfinfo`; static libraries and object files are located in `goo/`, `fofi/`, `xpdf/`.\n\n**Confirmed information:**\n\n* `xpdf/PDFDoc.h` contains the constructor `PDFDoc(BaseStream *strA, GString *ownerPassword = NULL, GString *userPassword = NULL, void *guiDataA = NULL)`.\n* `xpdf/GlobalParams.h` declares `extern GlobalParams *globalParams;` and constructor `GlobalParams(char *cfgFileName)`.\n* The `libhfuzz.h` header exists at `~/honggfuzz/libhfuzz/libhfuzz.h`.\n* The command to find `goo/Stream.h` did not find the file, so you must locate the correct definition of `MemStream` within the source tree yourself.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Read Source Before Writing\n\nRead:\n\n* `xpdf/pdfinfo.cc`\n* `xpdf/PDFDoc.h`\n* `xpdf/GlobalParams.h`\n* The headers/sources defining `BaseStream`, `MemStream`, `Object`, `GString`\n* `~/honggfuzz/libhfuzz/libhfuzz.h`\n* The current Makefile and Xpdf static libraries.\n\nAccurately determine the API and how `pdfinfo.cc` opens a PDF, checks document status, and frees resources.\n\nDo not guess header names, constructors, data types, or parameter order. Do not modify existing Xpdf source files.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Create `harness_ai.cc`\n\nCreate the file `harness_ai.cc` directly within the current workspace.\n\n**Requirements:**\n\n* C++ harness processes PDF data from an in-memory buffer, without writing the input to a temporary file.\n* Use `MemStream` and `PDFDoc` according to the actual API of Xpdf 3.02.\n* Use honggfuzz's persistent mode with `HF_ITER()` from `<libhfuzz/libhfuzz.h>`.\n* Initialize `globalParams` exactly once, outside the fuzzing loop.\n* Each iteration must create the necessary stream/document from the current input and free resources upon completion, even if the PDF is invalid.\n* Check whether the document opened successfully before accessing its structures.\n* Do not call `exit()` within the harness.\n* Do not modify Xpdf source files.\n* Safely handle empty or overly short inputs.\n* Perform PDF reading operations consistent with the execution path of `pdfinfo.cc`, within the scope of the available API.\n* Avoid memory leaks between iterations.\n* Add brief comments explaining the processing flow and resource ownership.\n\nIf an API cannot be verified from the source, continue investigating within the source tree instead of fabricating an API.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Compilation\n\nCreate a binary named `harness_hfuzz` in the current workspace.\n\nUse the compiler wrapper:\n`~/honggfuzz/hfuzz_cc/hfuzz-clang++`\n\nAccurately determine the static libraries and linking order from the existing Makefile/build. You may reuse previously built object files or static libraries if compatible, but ensure the final binary features honggfuzz instrumentation and supports persistent mode.\n\nDo not automatically switch to another fuzzing API if `HF_ITER()` works with the current honggfuzz version.\n\nRun the actual build command. If a build error occurs, read the error message, verify the cause, fix `harness_ai.cc` or the link command, and try again. Do not modify Xpdf source files to bypass errors.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Testing and Trial Run\n\nBefore fuzzing:\n\n* Verify that `~/xpdf-lab/corpus_pdf/seed.pdf` exists and is readable.\n* Verify that the `harness_hfuzz` binary was successfully created.\n* Check actual CLI options using `~/honggfuzz/honggfuzz --help`; do not guess syntax.\n* Run honggfuzz with a single worker (`-n 1`), an input corpus of `~/xpdf-lab/corpus_pdf`, and a 30-second run limit according to the syntax supported by the current binary.\n* Use a separate workspace/output directory so as not to overwrite the seed or other baseline data.\n* If a crash occurs, retain the artifact for inspection and reporting; do not hide or delete the crash.\n\nIf WSL/perf counters or the runtime environment prevent fuzzing from starting, report the exact error and troubleshooting steps; do not declare successful execution without evidence.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Final Report\n\nUpon completion, report:\n\n1. Files created or modified.\n2. The exact build command executed.\n3. Build results and instrumentation verification.\n4. The exact fuzzing command executed.\n5. Runtime, speed/exec/s, and number of crashes if displayed by the tool.\n6. Errors encountered and how they were resolved.\n7. A summary of how the harness receives input, creates `MemStream`, creates `PDFDoc`, processes the document, and frees resources.\n8. Unverified items, if any.\n\nDo not fabricate results. Perform the steps in the current workspace and only conclude success once actual results have been verified. ",
