          "type": "text",
          "text": "Done. Everything was built, linked, instrumented and actually fuzzed in the workspace.\n\n## 1. Files created / modified\n- **Created** `~/xpdf-lab/hfuzz/xpdf-3.02/harness_ai.cc` — the honggfuzz persistent-mode harness (new file, no Xpdf source touched).\n- **Created** `~/xpdf-lab/hfuzz/xpdf-3.02/harness_ai.o`, `~/xpdf-lab/hfuzz/xpdf-3.02/harness_hfuzz` (build artifacts).\n- **Created** `~/xpdf-lab/hfuzz/work30/` (honggfuzz workspace: crash artifacts + `run.log`), `~/xpdf-lab/hfuzz/work/`, `~/xpdf-lab/hfuzz/work_dbg/`, `~/xpdf-lab/hfuzz/out/`, `~/xpdf-lab/hfuzz/out30/` (new coverage corpus, 1817 files).\n- **Created** `/tmp/opencode/repro_check.cc` + binary (standalone verifier, outside the workspace).\n- **Modified**: nothing in `xpdf/`, `goo/`, `fofi/`, `splash/` (verified: `find -newermt` shows only the three new files). Seed corpus `~/xpdf-lab/corpus_pdf/seed.pdf` untouched (mtime 09:04, still only file present).\n\n## 2. Exact build commands\n```\ncd ~/xpdf-lab/hfuzz/xpdf-3.02\n~/honggfuzz/hfuzz_cc/hfuzz-clang++ -g -O0 -DHAVE_CONFIG_H -I. -Igoo -Ifofi -Isplash -Ixpdf \\\n  -c harness_ai.cc -o harness_ai.o\n\n~/honggfuzz/hfuzz_cc/hfuzz-clang++ -g -O0 -DHAVE_CONFIG_H -I. -Igoo -Ifofi -Isplash -Ixpdf \\\n  -o harness_hfuzz harness_ai.o \\\n  xpdf/Annot.o xpdf/Array.o xpdf/BuiltinFont.o xpdf/BuiltinFontTables.o xpdf/Catalog.o \\\n  xpdf/CharCodeToUnicode.o xpdf/CMap.o xpdf/Decrypt.o xpdf/Dict.o xpdf/Error.o \\\n  xpdf/FontEncodingTables.o xpdf/Function.o xpdf/Gfx.o xpdf/GfxFont.o xpdf/GfxState.o \\\n  xpdf/GlobalParams.o xpdf/JArithmeticDecoder.o xpdf/JBIG2Stream.o xpdf/JPXStream.o xpdf/Lexer.o \\\n  xpdf/Link.o xpdf/NameToCharCode.o xpdf/Object.o xpdf/Outline.o xpdf/OutputDev.o xpdf/Page.o \\\n  xpdf/Parser.o xpdf/PDFDoc.o xpdf/PDFDocEncoding.o xpdf/PSTokenizer.o xpdf/SecurityHandler.o \\\n  xpdf/Stream.o xpdf/UnicodeMap.o xpdf/XpdfPluginAPI.o xpdf/XRef.o \\\n  -Lgoo -lGoo -Lfofi -lfofi -lm\n```\nObject set = the `PDFINFO_OBJS` list from `xpdf/Makefile` minus `pdfinfo.o` (which owns `main()`); library order `-lGoo -lfofi -lm` is taken from `PDFINFO_LIBS`/`OTHERLIBS`. The pre-existing `goo/libGoo.a`, `fofi/libfofi.a` and the `xpdf/*.o` were reused — they are already honggfuzz-instrumented.\n\n## 3. Build result / instrumentation verification\n- Compile + link succeeded, `harness_hfuzz` = 3,555,752 bytes ELF PIE.\n- `nm harness_hfuzz | grep -c __sanitizer_cov` → 35 sancov symbols; `LIBHFUZZ_module_fetch` and `HF_ITER`/`HonggfuzzMain` present; the binary contains `_LIBHFUZZ_PERSISTENT_BINARY_SIGNATURE_` → honggfuzz logged *\"Persistent signature found in './harness_hfuzz'. Enabling persistent fuzzing mode\"*. Our `main` is the strong symbol (weak libhfuzz `main` overridden), so the `HF_ITER()` loop is what drives execution.\n\n## 4. Exact fuzzing command\n```\ncd ~/xpdf-lab/hfuzz/xpdf-3.02 && timeout 120 ~/honggfuzz/honggfuzz -n 1 --run_time 30 \\\n  -i ~/xpdf-lab/corpus_pdf -o ~/xpdf-lab/hfuzz/out30 -W ~/xpdf-lab/hfuzz/work30 -v -- ./harness_hfuzz\n```\n(options taken from `honggfuzz --help`: `-n/--threads`, `--run_time`, `-i/--input`, `-o/--output`, `-W/--workspace`, `-v`.)\n\n## 5. Runtime results (30 s run,1 worker)\n`Summary iterations:76942 time:31 speed:2482 crashes_count:15 timeout_count:4 new_units_added:1120 slowest_unit_ms:1042 guard_nb:12913 branch_coverage_percent:7 peak_rss_mb:241`\n- A separate 10 s sanity run gave: 30,107 iterations, speed 2737, 29 crashes.\n- 10 unique crash artifacts retained in `~/xpdf-lab/hfuzz/work30/` (plus 17 more in `~/xpdf-lab/hfuzz/work/`), all `SIGSEGV.PC.5555556a4485...INSTR.movsbl_(%rax),%eax.fuzz` (a second variant at `PC.5555556a8864`, `mov (%rax,%rcx,4),%esi`).\n- Symbolized with `addr2line -e harness_hfuzz` and reproduced standalone with `/tmp/opencode/repro_check`: the fault is inside **Xpdf itself**, not the harness —\n  `MemStream::getChar() Stream.h:325` ← `Object::streamGetChar` ← `Lexer::getChar` ← `Parser::Parser` ← `XRef::readXRef (XRef.cc:306)` ← `PDFDoc::setup (PDFDoc.cc:187)`; the second PC maps to `ObjectStream::getObject (XRef.cc:183)`.\n\n## 6. Errors encountered and how they were resolved\n1. **First link attempt failed**: `clang++: error: no such file or directory: 'xpdf/Annot.o xpdf/Array.o ...'` — the object list held in a shell variable was passed to the wrapper as one single argument. Fixed by writing the object list explicitly on the command line.\n2. **`EXITED, exit code: 1` persistent restarts (298 in the 30 s run)** — traced to `goo/gmem.cc:168` (`gmalloc` → \"Bogus memory allocation size\" → `exit(1)`) inside Xpdf's own allocator on malformed inputs. This is Xpdf-internal behaviour; the harness itself never calls `exit()`. Honggfuzz simply relaunches the persistent process.\n3. **Timeouts (4)**: default1 s per-input limit; honggfuzz SIGKILLs and relaunches the persistent process.\n4. **Initial \"could not find `goo/Stream.h`\"** — `MemStream`/`BaseStream` actually live in `xpdf/Stream.h` (verified: `xpdf/Stream.h:314` `class MemStream : public BaseStream`, ctor `MemStream(char *bufA, Guint startA, Guint lengthA, Object *dictA)` at `xpdf/Stream.cc:702`; `needFree = gFalse`, so the buffer is owned by the caller).\n\n## 7. Harness flow (summary)\n`main()` → `globalParams = new GlobalParams(cfgFileName)` once, `setErrQuiet(gTrue)` → infinite loop `HF_ITER(&buf,&len)` (honggfuzz hands over the next input from its shared mmap) → `processInput()`: copy bytes into a private `gmalloc` buffer (so the pointer stays valid and exactly sized) → `new MemStream(buf, 0, len, &dictObj)` → `new PDFDoc(str)` (PDFDoc takes ownership of the stream) → if `!doc->isOk()` → `delete doc; gfree(buf); return;` → otherwise the pdfinfo.cc-equivalent steps: `getDocInfo()` + Info-dict string decoding, `getStructTreeRoot()`, `getNumPages()`/crop & media boxes for at most 4 pages (`Catalog::getPage()` is not bounds-checked), `isEncrypted()/okTo*`, `isLinearized()`, `getPDFVersion()`, `readMetadata()` → `delete doc` (frees catalog, xref and the MemStream) → `gfree(buf)`. No `exit()`, no per-iteration leak.\n\n## 8. Unverified / caveats\n- The harness covers the **pdfinfo** path only (metadata/page tree/xref parsing). Page *content* rendering (Gfx/`pdftotext` path) is not exercised, per the requested scope.\n- `branch_coverage_percent: 7` is honggfuzz's estimate from its own instrumentation; not independently measured.\n- The crash artifacts are Xpdf 3.02 parser bugs (out-of-bounds read in `MemStream::getChar` reached from `XRef::readXRef`, and `ObjectStream::getObject`); I did not triage them further or determine CVE mapping. They are kept in `~/xpdf-lab/hfuzz/work*/`, not deleted or hidden.\n- `/tmp/opencode/repro_check.cc` is a throwaway verifier, outside the workspace; it is not part of the deliverable.",
